---
import BaseLayout from '~/components/BaseLayout.astro';
import DocsShell from '~/components/DocsShell.astro';
import CodeBlock from '~/components/CodeBlock.astro';
import Callout from '~/components/Callout.astro';
import { SITE, VERSIONS } from '~/data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Yeptris Ruby — YAML docs"
  description="The yeptris gem: Psych-compatible YAML for Ruby over libyeptris — FFI, no C extension, strict-JSON surface, Document node API, prebuilt platform gems."
>
  <DocsShell
    crumb="Yeptris — Ruby"
    title={`Yeptris — the YAML gem v${VERSIONS.yamlRuby}`}
    lede={`An FFI binding (no C extension, zero compilation at install) over libyeptris v${VERSIONS.yaml}. API shape and value semantics mirror Psych: YAML 1.1 implicit typing by default, the Psych error hierarchy, and a drop-in namespace.`}
  >
    <h2 id="install">Installation</h2>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`gem install yeptris`} />
    <p>
      RubyGems resolves a <strong>prebuilt platform gem</strong> where one
      exists: fat gems for x86_64/aarch64 Linux (glibc and musl), macOS
      (x86_64/arm64) and Windows (mingw and ucrt) — 14 release legs,
      lockstep-versioned with the engine. The gem binds the shared
      <code>libyeptris</code> through FFI: nothing compiles at install.
    </p>

    <h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="ruby"
      code={`require "yeptris"

Yeptris::YAML.load("name: yeptris\\nrating: 10\\n")
# => {"name" => "yeptris", "rating" => 10}

# Psych's YAML 1.1 implicit typing is the default (yes => true, 017 => 15);
# pass schema: :core_12 for YAML 1.2 core semantics
Yeptris::YAML.load(src, schema: :core_12)

Yeptris::YAML.dump({"name" => "yeptris", "tags" => [:yaml, :fast]})

begin
  Yeptris::YAML.load("a: [1,")
rescue Yeptris::ParseError => e
  e.message   # carries the C parser's line/column detail
end`}
    />
    <p>
      Dump builds through the library&rsquo;s DOM mutation API, so the C
      emitter&rsquo;s sizing, style-choosing and escape machinery applies
      to synthesized trees unchanged. Handles are document-scoped:
      <code>Document#free</code> releases everything in one C call, a GC
      finalizer backs it up, and any use after free raises
      <code>Yeptris::FreedError</code> — never a segfault.
    </p>

    <h2 id="json">The strict-JSON twin</h2>
    <p>
      <code>Yeptris::YAML.load</code> keeps the Psych contract for every
      input — including JSON-shaped ones (<code>&#123;&quot;a&quot;: [1,]&#125;</code>{" "}
      is legal flow YAML; <code>&quot;1e3&quot;</code> is a Psych String).
      <code>Yeptris::JSON.load</code> is the strict RFC 8259 surface —
      exact <code>JSON.parse</code> semantics by construction, spec-pinned
      value-by-value and error-by-error:
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="ruby"
      code={`require "yeptris/json"

Yeptris::JSON.load('{"a": [1, 2], "b": null, "c": 1e3}')
# => {"a" => [1, 2], "b" => nil, "c" => 1000.0}
# Bignum integers, exponent-only floats, duplicate-key semantics:
# every case shares JSON.parse's contract by test, not by claim.`}
    />

    <h2 id="document">The Document node API</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="ruby"
      code={`doc = Yeptris::Document.parse(config_yaml)
doc.root["server"]["port"].to_i
doc.serialize                    # canonical YAML through the C emitter
doc.free                         # one C call; FreedError afterwards`}
    />

    <h2 id="psych">Psych drop-in</h2>
    <p>
      <code>Yeptris::Psych</code> re-implements Psych&rsquo;s surface over
      the engine, and the error names consumers rescue are aliased at the
      top level — <code>Yeptris::DisallowedClass</code> is
      <code>Yeptris::Psych::DisallowedClass</code>. Informational notices
      are opt-in (<code>YEPTRIS_DEBUG=1</code>): a successful fallback is
      not a warning, and consumer CLIs that assert clean stderr stay clean
      by default.
    </p>
    <Callout kind="note">
      <p>
        Typing follows Psych&rsquo;s SafeLoader (YAML 1.1 implicit typing):
        <code>yes/no/on/off</code> booleans, <code>0x</code>/leading-0
        integers, merge keys, anchor identity. Every deliberate divergence
        from Psych is pinned by a spec — the conformance bar is Psych&rsquo;s
        own suite, ported.
      </p>
    </Callout>

    <h2 id="links">Where to go next</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href={`${SITE.githubYamlRuby}`}>leptris/yeptris-ruby</a> — the
        canonical repository and its platform matrix.
      </li>
      <li><a href="/docs/yeptris-getting-started">The C engine under the gem</a></li>
      <li><a href="/docs/yeptris-python">The Python sibling package</a></li>
      <li><a href="/benchmarks/yaml">The YAML benchmark campaigns</a></li>
    </ul>
  </DocsShell>
</BaseLayout>
